# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .ion/ — deny by default, allow only what is genuinely project config.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The root .ion/ is Ion's own working directory for this repo and fills up with
# ephemeral session state: plans, agent registries, memory, scratch, pid files,
# and whatever future Ion versions decide to put there. Only `commands/`,
# `skills/`, and `engine.json` are project configuration that every clone
# should receive; everything else is per-machine and must never be committed.
#
# Deny-by-default (rather than listing known-ephemeral paths) is deliberate: a
# new Ion subsystem that writes to .ion/ is ignored automatically instead of
# silently appearing in someone's `git status` months from now.
#
# Pattern order matters, and the middle line is load-bearing. Git will not
# re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded, so `!/.ion/` must
# re-admit the directory itself or every negation below it is dead — which is
# exactly the bug this replaces: `**/.ion/` alone made `!.ion/skills/` a no-op,
# so a NEW file under an allowed directory was invisible to `git status` and
# `git add` refused it without -f. Already-tracked files kept working only
# because .gitignore does not govern the index.
**/.ion/
!/.ion/
/.ion/*
!/.ion/commands/
!/.ion/skills/
!/.ion/engine.json

# Build output
node_modules/
dist/
out/
build/
release/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Stray Vite/electron-vite bundles emitted to the desktop root (hashed name).
# The normal output goes to out/; this guards against an accidental loose
# bundle being committed again (see the orphaned index-*.js removed in history).
desktop/index-*.js

# Go binaries
engine/bin/
engine/mcpserver
desktop/resources/engine/

# Gap analysis working files
engine/.gap-analysis/
engine/ion
relay/relay

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor / tool local state
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Claude Code project-scoped local settings
**/.claude/
# CLAUDE.md is a local-only symlink to AGENTS.md (the canonical, committed
# context file). Generated by scripts/setup-claude-symlinks.sh. Never commit.
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# Environment
.env
.env.*
.engine*.json

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Runtime
.ion.pid

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
.temp/

# Specs (untracked)
specs/
desktop/specs/
engine/specs
ios/specs
relay/specs

# iOS build artifacts
ios/DerivedData/
ios/build/

# Analysis
.analysis/

# E2E test config (contains API keys)
engine/tests/e2e/testconfig.json

docs/diagrams/
docs/responses/
docs/**/*.html

# graphify knowledge graph — a local build cache, not a source artifact.
#
# Not tracked, and the reason is workflow coupling rather than size. The bytes
# were never the problem: graph.json compresses ~22:1 and successive revisions
# delta to roughly 110 KB. Tracking it coupled a generated cache to the branch
# lifecycle, which made /create-pr and /squash abort on their own repo's
# automation (both refuse to run on a dirty tree, and the detached post-commit
# rebuild always dirties graphify-out/), and forced squash rules, review-scope
# exclusions, a merge driver, and a commit-cadence policy — all to manage a file
# that is 100% derived from tracked source and read by no build, test, or CI job.
#
# Rebuild it any time, offline and free: `graphify . --code-only`. Code
# extraction is pure local tree-sitter and community labels are LLM-free, so no
# API key is involved. `make bootstrap` builds it once on a fresh clone and the
# post-commit hook keeps it current from then on.
graphify-out/

# Editor/tool-local settings dropped by AI coding tools (e.g. grok CLI).
.grok/
